  "_notes": {
    "rho": "Stellarator rho is the volume radius sqrt(V_enclosed/V_plasma). The analytic surface-scaling parameter is internal only.",
    "Sw_override": "Plasma-facing surface area [m^2] for real machines (APPROX, confirm vs published). W7-X ~128 and LHD ~120 from published plasma-surface estimates; HSX 9.1 and CFQS 12.6 estimated from 2*pi*R0 * 2*pi*a * sqrt((1+kappa^2)/2) with kappa~1.5. Anchors Pwall=(Pfus+Pheat)/Sw instead of the extreme near-axis elongation profile (e.g. HSX elongation ~384). Concept reactors (HELIAS, NAE-QA) keep Sw_override=0 (pure near-axis). See docs/39.",
    "etabar": "For measured machines (W7-X/LHD/HSX/CFQS) etabar only sizes a single-harmonic near-axis cross-section for the SHAPE cartoon; the transform/volume/wall come from measured iota/Vp_override/Sw_override, so etabar does not affect their power account. Single-harmonic near-axis cannot truly represent these devices, so the derived near-axis diagnostics (iota_geom/kappa_eff/elong_max/helicity) are UNRELIABLE for them — e.g. W7-X gives iota_geom~2.07 (real ~0.88) and elongation ~10-14 (real ~1), LHD gives iota_geom=0 (planar axis). The UI flags these as '近轴估/est'. Use measured iota/Vp/Sw, not these estimates.",
    "shape": "Real machines carry an explicit 'shape' = truncated (|m|,|n|<=2), normalized boundary Fourier harmonics from a PUBLIC equilibrium (DESC desc/examples: W7-X, HSX, ESTELL; canonical l=2 heliotron for LHD), evaluated in DESC double-Fourier product basis and rescaled to preset R0 and a=R0/A. Cross-section VIEW only; near-axis cannot represent bean/heliotron/QA. Does NOT affect power account (iota/Vp/Sw measured). Truncated cartoon, not a full equilibrium.",
    "near_axis_presets": "precise-QA/precise-QH/QH-nfp3 are published near-axis quasisymmetry configs (pyQSC/Landreman-Paul 2022). Stored as concept presets: explicit rc/zs (axis Fourier, scaled by R0) + etabar (=|etabar_pub|/R0); NO measured overrides, so the near-axis engine computes iota/Vp/Sw self-consistently (iota matches published). Rendered via the second-order near-axis bean path."
  },
  "groups": {
    "实验装置 Experiments": [
      "W7-X",
      "LHD",
      "HSX",
